WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.498
The catalog configures integrations
through Microsoft Graph,

2
00:00:03.498 --> 00:00:07.988
and the book checked the older design's
permissions against Microsoft's reference.

3
00:00:07.988 --> 00:00:10.949
The operations were right;
the permissions weren't.

4
00:00:10.949 --> 00:00:15.658
One narrow permission, limited to applications
the connector owns, covers almost

5
00:00:15.658 --> 00:00:18.566
everything, and adding
the broad synchronization

6
00:00:18.566 --> 00:00:20.712
permission would undo that boundary.

7
00:00:20.712 --> 00:00:25.586
The real trap is assignment: the permission
it needs can grant anything to anyone,

8
00:00:25.586 --> 00:00:29.224
which turns the connector into
a privileged administrator.

9
00:00:29.224 --> 00:00:31.235
So it stays off the connector,

10
00:00:31.235 --> 00:00:35.675
and a person binds the access group
once, under a just-in-time role.

11
00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:38.975
After that, access changes
are just group membership.

12
00:00:38.975 --> 00:00:44.300
Every integration also has to land
correctly in the CMDB, so that's next.
